; A misspelled block header is reported once, and the indented lines
; beneath it are skipped along with it rather than reported one by one,
; as the remaining postings of a transaction that fails to parse are
; (issue #3260).  The journal is rejected either way, so nothing in the
; skipped block takes effect unnoticed; once the header is corrected, its
; sub-directives are read and checked.  --permissive does not change
; this: it quiets balance assertions, not syntax errors.

acount Assets:Cash
    note    Petty cash
    check   amount > 0

2024-01-01 Payee
    Expenses:Food    $10.00
    Assets:Cash

test bal -> 1
__ERROR__
While parsing file "$FILE", line 9:
Error: Unrecognized source line 'acount Assets:Cash'
end test

test --permissive bal -> 1
__ERROR__
While parsing file "$FILE", line 9:
Error: Unrecognized source line 'acount Assets:Cash'
end test
